## React Native Expo Best Practices

- Use functional components with hooks
- Utilize Expo SDK features and APIs
- Implement proper navigation using Expo Router
- Use Expo's asset system for images and fonts
- Implement proper error handling and crash reporting
- Utilize Expo's push notification system
- Use React Native Paper components for UI
- Implement proper offline support
- Use Expo's OTA updates for quick deployments
- Follow Expo Router conventions for file-based routing

## Expert Guidelines

### Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- Structure files: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, static content, types
- Follow Expo's official documentation for setup: https://docs.expo.dev/

### Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-wizard)
- Favor named exports for components

### TypeScript Usage
- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types
- Avoid enums; use maps instead
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig for type safety

### Syntax and Formatting
- Use the "function" keyword for pure functions
- Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals; concise syntax preferred
- Use declarative JSX
- Use Prettier for consistent code formatting

### UI and Styling
- Use Expo's built-in components for common UI patterns
- Implement responsive design with Flexbox and useWindowDimensions
- Use styled-components or Tailwind CSS for styling
- Support dark mode with useColorScheme
- Ensure accessibility using ARIA roles and native accessibility props
- Use react-native-reanimated and react-native-gesture-handler for animations

### Safe Area Management
- Use SafeAreaProvider from react-native-safe-area-context globally
- Wrap top-level components with SafeAreaView
- Use SafeAreaScrollView for scrollable content
- Avoid hardcoded padding/margins for safe areas

### Navigation
- Use react-navigation best practices (stack, tab, drawer)
- Leverage deep linking and universal links
- Use dynamic routes with expo-router

### Backend Integration
- Use Supabase as the primary database
- Secure serverless functions with Supabase MPC
- Use Sentry.io MPC for error monitoring

### Error Handling and Validation
- Use Zod for runtime validation and error handling
- Implement error logging with Sentry
- Use early returns and global error boundaries
- Handle errors at function start; avoid deep nesting

### Testing
- Write unit tests with Jest and React Native Testing Library
- Implement integration tests with Detox
- Use Expo's testing tools across environments
- Consider snapshot testing for UI consistency

### Security
- Sanitize inputs to prevent XSS
- Use react-native-encrypted-storage for sensitive data
- Ensure secure API communication with HTTPS
- Follow Expo's security guidelines: https://docs.expo.dev/guides/security/

### Internationalization
- Use expo-localization or react-native-i18n
- Support multiple languages and RTL layouts
- Ensure text scaling for accessibility

### Key Conventions
- Use Expo's managed workflow
- Prioritize Mobile Web Vitals (load time, responsiveness)
- Use expo-constants for configuration
- Use expo-permissions for device permissions
- Implement expo-updates for OTA updates
- Test compatibility on iOS and Android

### API Documentation
- Refer to Expo's docs: https://docs.expo.dev/

